(OrbitCare Workshop | Product and Engineering Release Dossier) Tj
T*
(Release 3.2.0 | October 28, 2026) Tj
T*
(Audience: facilities coordinators, technicians, and integration developers) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Release overview) Tj
T*
(OrbitCare is a fictional service console for tracking maintenance of shared workshop) Tj
T*
(equipment. Release 3.2 adds recurring inspection plans, an equipment history export, and) Tj
T*
(a read-only service endpoint. This dossier combines customer-facing facts with internal) Tj
T*
(notes; keep the distinction clear when preparing public material.) Tj
T*
T*
(2. Confirmed user changes) Tj
T*
(Inspection plans can be created for an equipment record with a cadence of weekly,) Tj
T*
(monthly, or quarterly. A plan assigns a checklist and a responsible team. When an) Tj
T*
(inspection is due, it appears in the team's work queue. The release does not describe) Tj
T*
(automatic calendar invitations.) Tj
T*
T*
(Equipment history can be downloaded as CSV by users with Coordinator access. The export) Tj
T*
(contains equipment label, event date, event type, work-order reference, and completion) Tj
T*
(state. Technician comments are excluded from the downloadable file. The report covers) Tj
T*
(one equipment record at a time.) Tj
T*
T*
(3. API addition) Tj
T*
(GET /api/v3/equipment/{equipment_id}/events returns recent events for one equipment) Tj
T*
(record. Authentication uses the existing workspace access token. Each result includes) Tj
T*
(event_id, occurred_at, event_type, and work_order_id. Results are ordered newest first,) Tj
T*
(with a default page size of 25 and a maximum page size of 100. The response includes) Tj
T*
(next_cursor when another page is available.) Tj
T*
T*
(The endpoint is read-only. Creating, editing, or deleting events through this endpoint) Tj
T*
(is not supported. API access must be enabled by a workspace administrator. The source) Tj
T*
(does not specify a public API availability SLA.) Tj
T*
T*
(4. Permission change) Tj
T*
(A new workspace setting, Allow external equipment links, controls whether Coordinators) Tj
T*
(can create a view-only link for an equipment record. The setting is off by default.) Tj
T*
(Workspace administrators can change it. A link does not grant access to the rest of the) Tj
T*
(workspace. Link expiry and revocation behavior are not specified in this release note) Tj
T*
(and should be confirmed before being documented.) Tj
T*
T*
(5. Engineering observations) Tj
T*
(An internal benchmark reported that the median load time for the equipment history page) Tj
T*
(fell from 1.8 seconds to 1.2 seconds across a sample of 400 requests in a staging) Tj
T*
(environment. This is an internal staging result, not a production guarantee. The test) Tj
T*
(did not measure cold-cache behavior or mobile networks.) Tj
T*
T*
(The background queue was changed to retry a failed inspection reminder twice, with a) Tj
T*
(five-minute delay between attempts. Engineering has not supplied delivery-rate) Tj
T*
(measurements. A reminder may still be delayed if the notification provider is) Tj
ET
