(unavailable.) Tj
T*
T*
(6. Security and privacy notes) Tj
T*
(The endpoint returns equipment event metadata only and requires a valid workspace token.) Tj
T*
(External links expose the equipment label and event dates to anyone who has the link,) Tj
T*
(when the workspace setting is enabled. Do not claim that linked records are private to) Tj
T*
(invited workspace members. The release dossier does not specify link entropy, expiry, or) Tj
T*
(audit logging for link views.) Tj
T*
T*
(7. Migration and compatibility) Tj
T*
(No database migration is required for hosted workspaces. Self-managed installations must) Tj
T*
(upgrade the API service and web application together. The minimum supported application) Tj
T*
(version for API clients is not listed. Clients should ignore response fields they do not) Tj
T*
(recognize; no compatibility window is promised.) Tj
T*
T*
(8. Items requiring confirmation) Tj
T*
(A planning note proposes QR-code labels, predictive maintenance, automatic parts) Tj
T*
(ordering, and a mobile technician app. These are roadmap ideas only and are not included) Tj
T*
(in version 3.2.0. Another draft says external links expire after 24 hours, but no) Tj
T*
(approved source confirms that statement. Do not publish either claim as fact.) Tj
T*
T*
(9. Customer-facing recap) Tj
T*
(Teams can schedule recurring equipment inspections, download a CSV history for an) Tj
T*
(individual asset, and retrieve recent event metadata through a read-only API endpoint.) Tj
T*
(Coordinators may share an equipment-specific view-only link only when an administrator) Tj
T*
(enables the setting. The benchmark and roadmap ideas should remain out of) Tj
T*
(customer-facing claims unless separately approved.) Tj
ET
